Copyright      : the patch file carries no separate copyright line, so no
                 holder is asserted here beyond the license above.

The file is stored unmodified. scripts/apply_sqlite_row_counts_patch.py applies
it to the SQLite 3.53.4 amalgamation, and the result is what Qenome compiles:
vendor/sqlite3/sqlite3.c and sqlite3.h. The script refuses a patch or an
amalgamation whose hash differs from the recorded ones.

The patch adds two prepared-statement counters to sqlite3_stmt_status():
  LIBSQL_STMTSTATUS_ROWS_READ      = 1025   rows read
  LIBSQL_STMTSTATUS_ROWS_WRITTEN   = 1026   rows written


libSQL counters
---------------
The patch's own comments call the counters a "libSQL extension", and their
names keep the LIBSQL_ prefix:
  https://github.com/tursodatabase/libsql
  License: MIT License, Copyright 2023 the sqld authors
  https://github.com/tursodatabase/libsql/blob/main/LICENSE.md

Which of the two upstreams the file text was copied from cannot be told from
the patch itself, so both are recorded: workerd distributes it, and the counters
it adds come from libSQL.
